    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "After the 2012 failure of Mitt Romney, around that time, there was this project known as the Reformicon Project, started by a lot of smart people, including people like Yivol Levin. I know that you've written for places that have published all these folks, and they engaged in this project. that was basically designed to try to solve some of the problems that you're talking about, but it really didn't catch on. They basically just became viewed as Democrat light and to the extent that their ideas were taken up in 2016, perhaps by, you know, mostly Marco Rubio, they really didn't connect with people. How is your vision different than theirs in terms of delivering on policy solutions for the working class as opposed to just talking about their importance?",
