    "turn_text": "Well, I do think it's a good thing and so far as I think we cannot be reliant, Republicans shouldn't be reliant on these woke capitalists in order to fund their campaigns or do anything else. We shouldn't be taking orders from our voters. And I think any shift that makes Republican, any elected official, but Republicans, the ones I care about that makes them more responsive to their voters is good. But just on the broader issue you touch on, Ben, I think what the voters understand is that the woke corporations are not with us. They have their own left-wing agenda that they are pushing for their own reasons and interests. And the reason, in many cases, is that the whole leadership class of these corporations, they are all very hardcore left woke capitalists. I mean, they buy into the progressive left-wing agenda and they're not afraid. to use their corporate power to push it and you see that right now in this fight over women's sports and you see the left wing of the heck not just the left wing the whole democrat party out there essentially advocating for the abolition of girls sports and women sports in america",
